<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Vision Encoder</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The vision encoder is initialized from InternViT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2024d</a>]</cite> and supports dynamic image tiling for variable resolution inputs, building upon the Vision Transformer (ViT) architecture <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dosovitskiy et al., 2020</a>]</cite>.
The encoder processes images at multiple scales, with maximum support for 4K resolution inputs.
We employ a tile-based approach where the image is divided into dynamic number of 448×448 pixel tiles, plus an additional global snapshot where the entire image is resized to 448×448 to help the model capture holistic image information.
The vision transformer configurations are as follows:</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.T3" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S2.T3.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S2.T3.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
